sidebar__version"><a class="documentation-sidebar__link" href="../changelog">v<!-- -->3.4.0</a></div></aside><main class="documentation-sidebar__content"><h1 class="bold" id="grid"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="grid#grid">Grid</a></h1>
<p>The main function of the grid is to distribute items to rows and columns.</p>
<p>Our grid has a maximum of 12 columns. Each column can have a <a href="grid#columns" class="underline">custom size</a>
defined by <a href="grid#breakpoints" class="underline">breakpoints</a>.</p>
<h2 class="bold" id="breakpoints"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="grid#breakpoints">Breakpoints</a></h2>
<p>Grid uses the mobile-first definition of <a href="../fundamentals/breakpoints" class="underline">breakpoints</a>, which means that smallest
breakpoint defines default size.</p>
<h2 class="bold" id="columns"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="grid#columns">Columns</a></h2>
<p>You can have a maximum of 12 columns in one row. A default column takes all the available
space.</p>
