<h3 class="bold" id="resizing"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="grid#resizing">Resizing</a></h3>
<p>There are two ways of resizing a column.</p>
<ol>
<li><span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">.grid__col--[size]</span></span></code></span> where <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">size</span></span></code></span> is a number 1-12 or one of <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">[shrink/fill/auto]</span></span></code></span></li>
<li><span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">.grid__col--[breakpoint]-[size]</span></span></code></span> where <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">breakpoint</span></span></code></span> is used as a <strong>minimum display width</strong> to change the column size</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>XS breakpoint size</strong></p>
<p>There is <strong>no need to specify the xs breakpoint size</strong> because it&#x27;s a default by definition of mobile-first philosophy.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 class="bold" id="what-is-shrinkfillauto"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="grid#what-is-shrinkfillauto">What is shrink/fill/auto?</a></h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">shrink</span></span></code></span> column takes <strong>the least amount of space</strong> available</li>
<li><span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">fill</span></span></code></span> column takes <strong>all the space</strong> available and <strong>does not shrink</strong> to accomodate other columns</li>
<li><span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">auto</span></span></code></span> takes <strong>all available space</strong>, also tries to <strong>shrink</strong> to fit into one row. This is the <strong>same as</strong> <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">.grid__col</span></span></code></span>.</li>
</ul>
